{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChUui4pJV1u8trdD3u8Vx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I added the starter LLM scanner `scanners/architecture`, and the `internal/roles`, `internal/initcmd` and `internal/config` tests pass. I did not run the full `make lint test`; I ran `gofmt` and `go vet` on the changed packages, and both were clean.\n\n- **Prompt:** `internal/roles/scanners/architecture/prompt.txt` covers the job, the order of reference docs, the UNTRUSTED fencing, the output schema, the `<rule>:<path>[:<symbol>]` fingerprint rules and two worked examples.\n- **Config:** the override in `internal/roles/config.yaml` uses Sonnet, every 3 days, max 3 open, groups of 1, a 20-minute timeout and `max_budget_usd: 2`. The loader accepted every key.\n- **Wiring:** the role is embedded in `internal/roles/roles.go`, and `internal/initcmd/body.go` adds a PR body bullet with the opt-out.\n- **Tests:** the new `internal/roles/architecture_test.go` checks the config load, the host-untrusted listing and the prompt contract. It also feeds the prompt's examples through `DecodeFindings` and `CheckLLMFingerprints`, and checks that bad fingerprints fail. I updated `internal/roles/roles_test.go` and `internal/initcmd/initcmd_test.go` to match.\n- **Docs:** I added `architecture` to the role lists in `docs/proposal.md`, `docs/layout.md` and `docs/site/roles/scanners.md`.\n\nThe prompt ships to every `ard init` adopter and runs unattended in host mode (#84), so a maintainer should read it before merge. Adding the scanner to this repository's own `.ard/` touches protected paths and is left to a human.\n\nThe report is in `.ard/52/worker-engineer.md`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":970,"cache_read_input_tokens":36534,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":970},"output_token